   "use": "Said when people share photos, mostly as kono shashin mite (look at this photo) while holding out a phone, or shashin mita? (did you see the photo I sent?). Casual speech drops o. Something you've only seen in pictures is shashin de mita.",
   "notes": "Asking to see someone's photos uses miseru: shashin misete (show me).",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "chotto kono shashin mite.",
    "ja": "ちょっとこの写真見て。",
    "english": "Take a look at this photo."
   },
   "examplePolite": {
    "romaji": "chotto kono shashin o mite kudasai.",
    "ja": "ちょっとこの写真を見てください。",
    "english": "Please take a look at this photo."
   }
  },
  {
