   ],
   "flags": [],
   "use": "Said about idly using a phone, usually in the -teru form: zutto sumaho ijitteru (always on their phone). About someone else it often carries a mild complaint; about yourself it admits a habit. Casual speech drops o.",
   "notes": "With a person as the object, ijiru means tease (slangy): ijiranaide yo (stop teasing me).",
   "example": {
    "romaji": "mata sumaho ijitteru.",
    "ja": "またスマホいじってる。",
    "english": "You're on your phone again."
